  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.5" extension="2015-08-01"/><templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.5.1" extension="2015-08-01"/>
    <code code="11450-4" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Problem List"/>
    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Elevated blood pressure at the first visit, 166/94 mmHg (average of two seated readings), without a previous diagnosis of hypertension; no symptoms; out-of-office confirmation with a week of home readings requested</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R03.0</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting finding at re-entry; superseded by the diagnosis at the second visit.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Essential hypertension, stage 2, confirmed by home readings averaging 154/90 mmHg; no left ventricular hypertrophy on ECG; urine albumin normal</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>I10</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis made at the second visit.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Right carotid bruit heard at the first visit in a man with no symptoms of stroke or transient ischemic attack; carotid duplex ultrasound and vascular neurology consultation requested</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R09.89</td><td>S — Synthetic examination finding; superseded by the duplex result at the second visit.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Asymptomatic atherosclerotic stenosis of the right internal carotid artery, 50 to 69 percent by duplex ultrasound, with less than 50 percent plaque on the left; no stroke or transient ischemic attack; managed with best medical therapy (blood pressure control, a statin and low-dose aspirin) and yearly duplex surveillance</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>I65.21</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis made at the vascular neurology consultation; not a claim about his real arteries.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-5">
    <td>Recent release from about six years of incarceration: re-entering community life on parole at 65, establishing primary care with no medical records yet received, a rented room, no earned income, and a public reputation he feels as a burden</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z65.2</td><td>S — Synthetic modern social problem anchored to his documented imprisonment and parole.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

